Fixed. The problem was that pip's source code had been deleted from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/` — only the `.dist-info` metadata remained. I restored it by extracting the bundled wheel (`pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl`) from the `ensurepip/_bundled` directory. `pip3` is now fully functional and can install packages.

